    ],
    cons: [
      "Does not fold",
      "The listing does not say what data reaches the Peloton App, so expect to set speed by hand",
      "About $935 on Amazon, more than the T101 Connect",
    ],
    bottomLine: "The treadmill to buy for Peloton running classes: it matches the Tread’s ranges closely for a fraction of the price.",
    description: "The Horizon 7.0 AT is our best overall pick because it covers Peloton’s running classes and makes the constant speed changes easy. Our spec-checked review gives a 20 by 60-inch deck, 0.5 to 12 mph, 0 to 15% incline and a 325 lb capacity, with Bluetooth FTMS. The Amazon listing adds QuickDial speed and incline controls with Rapid Sync for faster changes, 3-zone variable response cushioning, and app compatibility that names Peloton, Strava and Zwift, with a note that separate subscriptions are required. It does not fold, and the listing does not explain what the Peloton connection shares, so plan on changing speed and incline yourself. Amazon showed it at $934.98 on 21 November 2026.",
  },
  {
    id: "horizon-t101-connect",
    name: "Horizon T101 Connect",
    brand: "Horizon",
    category: "Peloton App on a Budget",
    badge: "Best Value",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0F9LQY1P4?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31pAWKay09L._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":500},
    reviewUrl: "/horizon-t101-treadmill/",
    priceRange: "About $777 (Amazon, 21 Nov 2026)",
    priceBounds: {"low":777,"high":777},
    specs: "20 x 55 in. deck · 0.5–10 mph · up to 10% incline · device holder · lifetime frame and motor (listing)",
    pros: [
      "Names JRNY, Peloton and Zwift as compatible apps on its listing",
      "A built-in device holder for a phone or tablet",
      "EasyDial controls and one-touch keys for intervals",
      "Lifetime frame and motor warranty, and it folds",
    ],
    cons: [
      "Tops out at 10 mph and 10%, short of the Tread’s 12.5 and 12.5",
      "A 55-inch deck is tight for taller runners at speed",
      "Fine for walking, hiking and jogging classes; limited for sprint intervals",
    ],
    bottomLine: "The pick for walkers and joggers who want Peloton classes on a folding treadmill for under $800.",
    description: "The T101 Connect is the value pick because its Amazon listing names Peloton among its compatible apps and it has the device holder the app needs, for about $777. The listing gives a 20 by 55-inch running area with 3-zone variable response cushioning, power incline up to 10% and speeds from 0.5 to 10 mph, EasyDial controls with one-touch keys, a Bluetooth heart-rate receiver and contact grips, Bluetooth speakers, a USB charging port, a fan and a device holder. It folds, and Horizon gives lifetime frame and motor cover. The limits are the 10 mph and 10% ceilings, which will cap you in fast interval classes. Amazon showed it at $777.36 on 21 November 2026.",
  },
  {
    id: "horizon-t202",
    name: "Horizon T202",
    brand: "Horizon",
    category: "Folding Treadmill for Running Classes",
    badge: "Best Folding",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0BHZVT9T6?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/310lm1txGhL._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":342},
    reviewUrl: "/horizon-t202-treadmill/",
    priceRange: "About $800 (Amazon, 21 Nov 2026)",
    priceBounds: {"low":800,"high":800},
    specs: "60 x 20 in. running area · up to 12 mph · 12% incline · 325 lb · device holder · hydraulic fold (listing)",
    pros: [
      "12 mph and 12% on a folding frame",
      "A 60-inch deck, longer than the T101’s",
      "A holder for your device to stream classes, per the listing",
      "EasyDial controls: roll forward for speed, the other dial for incline",
    ],
    cons: [
      "The listing does not name Peloton specifically",
      "Assembled footprint of 76 x 34 x 57 inches is still large when unfolded",
      "Incline stops at 12%, below the 15% of the 7.0 AT and Sole F65",
    ],
    bottomLine: "The folding pick for runners: 12 mph and a 60-inch deck, with somewhere to put the screen.",
    description: "The T202 is our folding pick because it reaches 12 mph on a 60-inch deck and still folds away. The Amazon listing gives a 60 by 20-inch running area, 12% incline, a 12 mph top speed and a 325 lb capacity, with a hydraulic folding system and an assembled size of 76 by 34 by 57 inches. It describes pairing your device with the Bluetooth speakers and placing it on the holder to stream workout classes, with EasyDial controls for speed and incline. Its listing does not name Peloton, but nothing about the Peloton App needs it to: you stream the class on your device and use the dials. Amazon showed it at $799.99 on 21 November 2026.",
  },
  {
    id: "sole-f65",
    name: "Sole F65",
    brand: "Sole",
    category: "Closest to the Tread’s Speed and Incline",
    badge: "Closest to the Tread",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0HFSZR19W?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31qNRVPVU1L._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":500},
    reviewUrl: "/sole-f65-treadmill/",
    priceRange: "About $1,200 (Amazon, 21 Nov 2026)",
    priceBounds: {"low":1200,"high":1200},
    specs: "3.25 HP · 0.5–12 mph · 0–15% power incline · 20 x 60 in. deck · folding · freight, curbside (listing)",
    pros: [
      "12 mph and 15% incline, above the Tread’s 12.5% incline",
      "A 20 by 60-inch cushioned deck",
      "Works without a paid app; Sole’s own app is optional",
      "Folds with a hydraulic cylinder",
    ],
    cons: [
      "The listing mentions no tablet holder; check the console shelf for your device",
      "Ships freight with curbside delivery only, per the listing",
      "The most expensive pick here",
    ],
    bottomLine: "The treadmill to buy if you want a machine that will never be the limit in a Peloton class.",
    description: "The Sole F65 is on this list for its figures: 0.5 to 12 mph and a 0 to 15% power incline on a 20 by 60-inch cushioned deck, which covers every speed a Peloton class asks for and more incline than the Tread itself. The Amazon listing gives a 3.25 HP motor, roller controls, hill, interval and strength programs, a kick-release fold with a hydraulic cylinder, dual Bluetooth speakers, a cooling fan, USB-C charging and Sole’s own app with smartwatch syncing. It does not mention a device holder, so check the console shelf fits your tablet. The listing says it ships freight with curbside service only. Amazon showed it at $1,199.99 on 21 November 2026; our F65 review has more on the frame and warranty.",
  },
  {
    id: "sole-f50",
    name: "Sole F50",
    brand: "Sole",
    category: "One-Touch Keys for Interval Classes",
    badge: "Best Quick Keys",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0HFSNMP16?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31jT2QJvdZL._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":333},
    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "About $900 (Amazon, 21 Nov 2026)",
    priceBounds: {"low":900,"high":900},
    specs: "Brushless motor · 0.5–10 mph · 12 power incline levels · quick keys at 3, 6 and 9 · 20 x 55 in. · 300 lb (listing)",
    pros: [
      "Quick-touch keys at 3, 6 and 9 plus dial-style speed and incline controls",
      "A quiet brushless motor, per the listing",
      "Folds with gas-shock assist and rolls away",
      "A 300 lb capacity and an 18 mm cushioned deck",
    ],
    cons: [
      "Tops out at 10 mph",
      "Incline is given as 12 levels, not a percentage",
      "A 55-inch deck suits walkers and joggers more than runners",
    ],
    bottomLine: "The pick for walkers and joggers who mostly take interval and hiking classes and want to change pace without looking down.",
    description: "The Sole F50 earns its place with its controls. The Amazon listing gives dial-style speed and incline controls plus quick-touch keys at 3, 6 and 9, which is exactly what a Peloton interval class needs: jump to a pace without counting button presses. It has a brushless motor running from 0.5 to 10 mph, 12 levels of power incline, a 20 by 55-inch running surface on an 18 mm cushioned deck, a 300 lb capacity, Bluetooth speakers, Sole’s app, 12 programs, USB-C charging and a fan, and it folds with gas-shock assist. The 10 mph ceiling and 55-inch deck make it a walking and jogging machine. Amazon showed it at $899.99 on 21 November 2026.",
  },
  {
    id: "aeriflo-x-t510a",
    name: "Aeriflo X-T510A Treadmill",
    brand: "Aeriflo",
    category: "12 mph for Under $650",
    badge: "Best Budget",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0GVMZR42Y?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41HmqiefNRL._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":500},
    reviewUrl: "/best-treadmills-with-kinomap/",
    priceRange: "About $627 (Amazon, 20 Nov 2026)",
    priceBounds: {"low":627,"high":627},
    specs: "3.5 HP · up to 12 mph · 20% powered incline · 55 x 20 in. belt · folding · 5-yr motor, 2-yr machine warranty (listing)",
    pros: [
      "The cheapest pick that reaches 12 mph",
      "A 20% incline, steeper than any Peloton class asks for",
      "Wireless phone charging on the console",
      "Hydraulic soft-drop fold",
    ],
    cons: [
      "The listing gives no maximum user weight",
      "A newer brand with a short track record",
      "Names Kinomap and FitShow, not Peloton",
    ],
    bottomLine: "The budget way to cover Peloton’s running classes, if you can confirm the weight limit with the seller.",
    description: "The Aeriflo X-T510A is the budget pick because it reaches 12 mph and a 20% incline for about $627, more range than any Peloton class needs. The Amazon listing gives a 3.5 HP motor, a 55 by 20-inch multi-layer belt, a soft-drop hydraulic fold, wireless phone charging, Bluetooth speakers, and a stated 5-year motor and 2-year machine warranty. It names Kinomap and FitShow rather than Peloton, which does not matter for streaming classes on your own device. The gap is the maximum user weight, which the listing does not state. We cover it in more detail in our best treadmills with Kinomap. Amazon showed it at $626.99 on 20 November 2026.",
  },
];

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      itemListElement: [
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Best Treadmills", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/best/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 3, name: "Best Treadmills for the Peloton App", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/best-treadmills-for-peloton-app/" },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      mainEntity: [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Can you use the Peloton App on any treadmill?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Yes. The Peloton App streams classes on a phone, tablet or TV, and you follow the instructor by setting the treadmill's speed and incline yourself. It does not need a Peloton Tread, and on other treadmills the app does not control the machine.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "What is the best treadmill for the Peloton App?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "For most people, the Horizon 7.0 AT: 12 mph, 15% incline and a 20 by 60-inch deck for about $935 on Amazon in November 2026, with Peloton named on its listing. For less, the Horizon T101 Connect at about $777, which stops at 10 mph and 10% incline.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Which Peloton membership do I need for a regular treadmill?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "App+ if treadmill classes are the main use; it was $28.99 a month or $289 a year on Peloton's site on 21 November 2026. App One was $12.99 a month but limited to three cardio equipment classes a month. Check Peloton's current prices before signing up.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Does the Peloton App track my treadmill speed?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Not from most treadmills. You enter effort by following the class, and the app can read a Bluetooth heart-rate monitor. Some Horizon listings name Peloton as a compatible app but do not say what data passes, so plan to set speed and incline by hand.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Is a treadmill plus the Peloton App cheaper than a Peloton Tread?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Usually by a wide margin. The treadmills here cost about $627 to $1,200 on Amazon in November 2026, and App+ costs less a month than the Tread's All-Access Membership. You give up the built-in screen and on-screen metrics.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "What speed and incline do Peloton treadmill classes need?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "The Peloton Tread runs to 12.5 mph and 12.5% incline, so a treadmill that reaches about 12 mph and 12 to 15% covers nearly every class. A 10 mph, 10% machine handles walking, hiking and most jogging classes but will cap you in fast intervals.",
          },
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: title,
      description: description,
      author: { "@type": "Person", "@id": "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/editorial-standards/#shaheer-ali-khan", name: "Shaheer Ali Khan", honorificSuffix: "PhD", jobTitle: "Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist", url: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/editorial-standards/#who", sameAs: ["https://www.linkedin.com/in/shaheer-ali-khan-data/"], worksFor: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Treadmill Reviews USA" } },
      datePublished: "2026-11-21",
      dateModified: "2026-11-21",
      publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Treadmill Reviews USA" },
    },
    ...PRODUCTS.map((product) => ({
      "@type": "Product",
      name: product.name,
      description: product.description,
      ...(product.brand ? { brand: { "@type": "Brand", name: product.brand } } : {}),
      ...(product.image ? { image: product.image.url } : {}),
      ...(product.priceBounds
        ? {
            offers: {
              "@type": "AggregateOffer",
              priceCurrency: "USD",
              lowPrice: product.priceBounds.low,
              highPrice: product.priceBounds.high,
              url: product.amazonUrl,
            },
          }
        : {}),
    })),
    {
      "@type": "ItemList",
      name: title,
      numberOfItems: 6,
      itemListElement: PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => ({
        "@type": "ListItem",
        position: index + 1,
        name: product.name,
        url: `https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/best-treadmills-for-peloton-app/#${product.id}`,
      })),
    },
  ],
};

// "More in" links: the other pages in this article's hub group.
const HERE = "/best-treadmills-for-peloton-app/";
const HUB = SECTIONS.find((s) => s.slug === "best");
const GROUP = HUB?.groups.find((g) => g.pages.some((p) => p.url === HERE)) ?? HUB?.groups[0];
const MORE = (GROUP?.pages ?? []).filter((p) => p.url !== HERE).slice(0, 6);
---

<Layout
  title={`${title} | Treadmill Reviews USA`}
  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  article={{
    publishedTime: "2026-11-21",
    modifiedTime: "2026-11-21",
    author: "Shaheer Ali Khan",
    section: "Fitness Equipment",
    tags: [
      "best treadmill for peloton app",
      "treadmill for peloton app",
      "peloton app treadmill",
      "peloton app on any treadmill",
      "peloton tread alternative",
      "treadmill compatible with peloton app",
    ],
  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
  stickyCta={{ text: "Best Overall: Horizon 7.0 AT", link: PRODUCTS[0].amazonUrl }}
>
  <article class="ed-article" data-template="editorial">
    <div class="ed-col">
      <nav class="ed-crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/best/">Best Treadmills</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true">›</span>
        <span>Buying Guide</span>
      </nav>
      <h1 class="ed-title">Best Treadmills for the Peloton App</h1>
      <p class="ed-dek">
        You do not need a Peloton Tread to take Peloton’s treadmill classes. The app runs on a phone or tablet beside any treadmill, and you set the speed and incline the instructor calls. What matters is a machine that can keep up with those calls, is easy to change mid-stride, and gives your screen somewhere to sit. Here are six, from $627 to about $1,200.
      </p>
      <p class="ed-answer"><strong>Short answer.</strong> Best Overall: <a href="#horizon-7-0-at">Horizon 7.0 AT</a>. Best Value: <a href="#horizon-t101-connect">Horizon T101 Connect</a>. Best Folding: <a href="#horizon-t202">Horizon T202</a>.</p>

      <!-- Byline -->
      <div class="ed-byline">
        <img src="/authors/shaheer-ali-khan.png" alt="Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD" width="44" height="44" />
        <div class="ed-byline-text">
          By <a href="/editorial-standards/#who" rel="author">Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD</a><br />
          Updated November 21, 2026 · Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist · ACSM-EP, CSCS<br />
          <span class="ed-method">How we chose: makers’ published specifications and manuals, independent reviews and owner reports, cross-checked. Not tested hands-on.</span>
        </div>
        <a href="#top-picks" class="btn-ghost">View products</a>
      </div>
      <p class="ed-disclosure">
        We may earn a commission when you buy through the links below. It costs you nothing and never decides a ranking. <a href="/editorial-standards/">How we review.</a>
      </p>

      <figure class="ed-hero">
        <div class="ed-hero-collage">
          <a href="#horizon-7-0-at"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/314wh+sUlyL._SL500_.jpg" alt="Horizon 7.0 AT" width="500" height="500" decoding="async" /></a>
          <a href="#horizon-t101-connect"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31pAWKay09L._SL500_.jpg" alt="Horizon T101 Connect" width="500" height="500" decoding="async" /></a>
          <a href="#horizon-t202"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/310lm1txGhL._SL500_.jpg" alt="Horizon T202" width="500" height="342" decoding="async" /></a>
        </div>
        <figcaption>Horizon 7.0 AT · Horizon T101 Connect · Horizon T202</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div class="ed-body prose prose-lg">
        <p class="ed-lead">
          The best treadmill for the Peloton App for most people is the Horizon 7.0 AT: a 20 by 60-inch
          deck, 12 mph, incline to 15%, quick-change dials, and an Amazon listing that names Peloton
          among the apps it works with, for about $935. If the budget is nearer $775, the Horizon T101
          Connect names Peloton too and has a device holder, though it stops at 10 mph and 10%. The
          reason to do this at all is money: a Peloton Tread costs thousands, and the app costs a
          fraction of the Tread&rsquo;s membership. We have not tested these treadmills hands-on. Each
          pick was chosen from its Amazon listing and our own spec-checked reviews, and each card says
          where its figures come from.
        </p>

        <section id="top-picks" class="ed-toppicks not-prose">
          <h2>Our top picks:</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Best Overall:</span> <a href="#horizon-7-0-at">Horizon 7.0 AT</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[0].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Best Value:</span> <a href="#horizon-t101-connect">Horizon T101 Connect</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[1].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Best Folding:</span> <a href="#horizon-t202">Horizon T202</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[2].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Closest to the Tread:</span> <a href="#sole-f65">Sole F65</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[3].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Best Quick Keys:</span> <a href="#sole-f50">Sole F50</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[4].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Best Budget:</span> <a href="#aeriflo-x-t510a">Aeriflo X-T510A Treadmill</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[5].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <nav class="ed-toc not-prose" aria-label="In this roundup">
          <h2>In this roundup</h2>
          <ol>
            <li><a href="#quick-picks">The short answer</a></li>
            <li><a href="#picks">The 6 picks</a></li>
            <li><a href="#how-it-works">How the Peloton App Works on Any Treadmill</a></li>
            <li><a href="#what-to-look-for">What to Look For in a Treadmill for Peloton Classes</a></li>
            <li><a href="#class-types">Which Peloton Classes Each Treadmill Can Handle</a></li>
            <li><a href="#vs-tread">Peloton Tread vs a Treadmill Plus the App</a></li>
            <li><a href="#setup">Setting Up Peloton Classes on Your Treadmill</a></li>
            <li><a href="#faq">Frequently asked questions</a></li>
          </ol>
        </nav>

        <div id="quick-picks" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Best Treadmill for the Peloton App: The Short Answer</h2>
<p>
            <strong>Buy the Horizon 7.0 AT if you run and want a machine that matches the Peloton
            Tread&rsquo;s speed and incline ranges; buy the Horizon T101 Connect if you mostly walk and jog
            and want to spend less; buy the Horizon T202 if it has to fold.</strong> The <a href="/sole-f65-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>Sole F65</a> is the
            closest match to the Tread&rsquo;s figures, the Sole F50 has the most useful quick keys, and the
            Aeriflo X-T510A is the cheapest machine here that reaches 12 mph.
          </p>
          <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto my-8"><table class="min-w-[640px] w-full text-sm border-collapse">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Treadmill</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Price seen</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Speed</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Incline</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Deck</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Peloton named?</th>
              </tr>
