          <details>
            <summary><h3>Does the Peloton App track my treadmill speed?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Not from most treadmills. You enter effort by following the class, and the app can read a Bluetooth heart-rate monitor. Some Horizon listings name Peloton as a compatible app but do not say what data passes, so plan to set speed and incline by hand.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Is a treadmill plus the Peloton App cheaper than a Peloton Tread?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Usually by a wide margin. The treadmills here cost about $627 to $1,200 on Amazon in November 2026, and App+ costs less a month than the Tread's All-Access Membership. You give up the built-in screen and on-screen metrics.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What speed and incline do Peloton treadmill classes need?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              The Peloton Tread runs to 12.5 mph and 12.5% incline, so a treadmill that reaches about 12 mph and 12 to 15% covers nearly every class. A 10 mph, 10% machine handles walking, hiking and most jogging classes but will cap you in fast intervals.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

